---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Crumbs from '../components/Crumbs.astro';
import { biz } from '../lib/site';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../lib/schema';
const path = '/privacy/';
const trail = [{ name: 'Privacy', path }];
const updated = 'October 2026';
---
<Layout title="Privacy Policy | Paws 2 Purrs" description="How Paws 2 Purrs uses the information you send through the website enquiry form, under UK GDPR." path={path} schema={[breadcrumbSchema(trail)]}>
  <Crumbs trail={trail} />
  <section class="section section--tight bg-cream">
    <div class="wrap wrap--narrow prose">
      <p class="label">Privacy</p>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p><em>Last updated: {updated}</em></p>
      <p>This policy explains how {biz.name} ("Paws 2 Purrs", "we") collects and uses your personal data when you use this website or get in touch. It's written to meet the UK General Data Protection Regulation (UK GDPR) and the Data Protection Act 2018.</p>

      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>Paws 2 Purrs is run by {biz.owner}, based in {biz.address.display}. You can contact us on {biz.phone.display}{biz.email ? ` or ${biz.email}` : ''}. We are the "controller" of the personal data described here.</p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>When you send the enquiry form, we collect what you choose to give us: your name, mobile number, email address (optional), area or postcode, preferred contact method, the service and dates you need, and details about your pet (name, breed, age and any notes, such as medication or behaviour).</p>
      <p>If you call, text, WhatsApp or email us, we receive your number or address and anything you tell us in your message.</p>

      <h2>Why we use it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To reply to your enquiry and arrange a meet &amp; greet (our lawful basis is taking steps at your request before entering into a contract).</li>
        <li>To look after your pet safely if you book with us, including health and behaviour notes you share (contract, and our legitimate interest in caring for your pet properly).</li>
        <li>To keep records we're required to keep as a licensed animal business (legal obligation).</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We will never sell your data or use it for marketing you haven't asked for.</p>

      <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
      <p>Form submissions are processed and stored by our website host, Netlify, Inc., which may store data outside the UK under appropriate safeguards. If you contact us on WhatsApp, Meta's terms also apply. We don't share your data with anyone else unless the law requires it, or in an emergency involving your pet (for example, with a vet).</p>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>If you don't go ahead with a booking, we delete enquiry details within 12 months. If you become a client, we keep your details for as long as we look after your pet and for a reasonable period afterwards to meet licensing and insurance requirements.</p>

      <h2>Cookies and analytics</h2>
      <p>This site doesn't use advertising cookies. The map only loads Google Maps (which may set cookies) if you click to load it. {biz.analytics.ga4Id ? 'We use Google Analytics to understand how people use the site, with data collected in aggregate.' : 'We may add Google Analytics in future to see, in aggregate, how people use the site; this policy will be updated if we do.'} The site remembers if you close the announcement bar, using your browser's local storage.</p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>You can ask to see, correct or delete the personal data we hold about you, object to how we use it, or ask us to stop using it. Just contact us. If you're unhappy with how we've handled your data, you can complain to the Information Commissioner's Office at <a href="https://ico.org.uk" rel="noopener" target="_blank">ico.org.uk</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
